        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $H$ be the number of heads. Interchanging heads and tails pairs the outcomes with at least five heads and those with at most four heads. Each pair has equal probability. These two events cover all outcomes and do not overlap.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(H\\geq5)&=\\frac{1}{2}\\bigl[P(H\\geq5)+P(H\\leq4)\\bigr]\\\\P(H\\geq5)&=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
